The problem: minimum number of operations to get n 'A's. Classic solution: sum of prime factors of n. For n = 1, answer is 0.

Approach: For each i from 2 while i*i <= n, while n % i == 0, add i to result and divide n by i. If n > 1 at the end, add n.

Let me write the PHP code:

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer $n
     * @return Integer
     */
    function minSteps($n) {
        $ans = 0;
        $d = 2;
        while ($d * $d <= $n) {
            while ($n % $d == 0) {
                $ans += $d;
                $n = intdiv($n, $d);
            }
            $d++;
        }
        if ($n > 1) {
            $ans += $n;
        }
        return $ans;
    }
}
```

