- Maintain a sliding window of the last `m` elements (queue).
- To remove the smallest `k` and largest `k` efficiently, use two Fenwick (Binary Indexed) trees over the value range `1..100000`: one for counts, one for sums.
- The answer is `(sum of smallest (m-k) elements − sum of smallest k elements) / (m − 2k)`, floored.
- "Sum of smallest t elements" is found via binary lifting on the count tree (find largest prefix position with count < t), then add the remaining needed copies of the next value.

