Looking at this problem:

**Approach:**
1. Sort flowers ascending. Gardens already ≥ `target` are automatically complete (a suffix in sorted order); let `idx` be the first index with `flowers[i] >= target`.
2. Enumerate `k` = number of *below-target* gardens we raise to `target`. By an exchange argument, these should be the `k` **largest** below-target gardens (completing a smaller garden while leaving a larger one incomplete never helps — swapping roles preserves cost and the incomplete multiset). Their cost is `k*target - sum of those values` (prefix sums), which is increasing in `k`, so we can break when it exceeds `newFlowers`.
3. With remaining budget `rem`, the incomplete gardens are the prefix `v[0..j-1]` (`j = idx-k`). Maximize their minimum level `L ≤ target-1`. Since `cost(L) = Σ max(0, L - v[i])` is non-decreasing in `L`, and `g(t) = t*v[t] - pre[t]` (cost to raise first `t` gardens to level `v[t]`, with `g(j) = j*cap - pre[j]`) is non-decreasing, binary search the largest `t` with `g(t) ≤ rem`. Then `L = cap` if `t = j`, else `L = max(v[t], min(upper, floor((rem+pre[t+1])/(t+1))))` where `upper = v[t+1]` (or `cap` if `t+1 = j`).
4. Beauty for this `k` is `(n-j)*full + L*partial` (L=0 when `j=0`). Take the max over all feasible `k`.

Verified against both examples (14 and 30) and several edge cases (all complete already, single garden, duplicates, huge budgets).

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[] $flowers
     * @param Integer $newFlowers
     * @param Integer $target
     * @param Integer $full
     * @param Integer $partial
     * @return Integer
     */
    function maximumBeauty($flowers, $newFlowers, $target, $full, $partial) {
        sort($flowers);
        $n = count($flowers);

        $pre = array_fill(0, $n + 1, 0);
        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
            $pre[$i + 1] = $pre[$i] + $flowers[$i];
        }

        $lo = 0;
        $hi = $n;
        while ($lo < $hi) {
            $mid = ($lo + $hi) >> 1;
            if ($flowers[$mid] >= $target) {
                $hi = $mid;
            } else {
                $lo = $mid + 1;
            }
        }
        $idx = $lo;

        $cap = $target - 1;
        $ans = 0;

        for ($k = 0; $k <= $idx; $k++) {
            $cost = $k * $target - ($pre[$idx] - $pre[$idx - $k]);
            if ($cost > $newFlowers) {
                break;
            }
            $rem = $newFlowers - $cost;
            $j = $idx - $k;

            if ($j == 0) {
                $minLevel = 0;
            } else {
                $lo = 0;
                $hi = $j;
                while ($lo < $hi) {
                    $mid = ($lo + $hi + 1) >> 1;
                    if ($mid < $j) {
                        $g = $mid * $flowers[$mid] - $pre[$mid];
                    } else {
                        $g = $j * $cap - $pre[$j];
                    }
                    if ($g <= $rem) {
                        $lo = $mid;
                    } else {
                        $hi = $mid - 1;
                    }
                }
                $t = $lo;
                if ($t == $j) {
                    $minLevel = $cap;
                } else {
                    $t1 = $t + 1;
                    $upper = ($t1 < $j) ? $flowers[$t1] : $cap;
                    $cand = intdiv($rem + $pre[$t1], $t1);
                    if ($cand > $upper) {
                        $cand = $upper;
                    }
                    if ($flowers[$t] > $cand) {
                        $cand = $flowers[$t];
                    }
                    $minLevel = $cand;
                }
            }

            $beauty = ($n - $j) * $full + $minLevel * $partial;
            if ($beauty > $ans) {
                $ans = $beauty;
            }
        }

        return $ans;
    }
}
```

