This is a classic binary search on answer problem.

Approach:
- If m * k > n, return -1 (need more flowers than available). Careful with overflow — in PHP integers are 64-bit so m*k up to 10^6 * 10^5 = 10^11, fine.
- Binary search on days between min(bloomDay) and max(bloomDay).
- For a given day d, count how many bouquets can be made: iterate through bloomDay, count consecutive bloomed flowers; each time count reaches k, increment bouquets and reset count. If bouquets >= m, feasible.

