Looking at this problem:

- `n ≤ 14` → bitmask DP over `2^n` states.
- For each mask, keep the best pair `(sessions used, remaining time in current open session)`. Fewer sessions is better; for equal sessions, more remaining time is better (it dominates: any future completion from a state with fewer sessions, or equal sessions with more remaining, needs no more total sessions — this dominance is preserved when adding any task: if a task fits the current session we place it, otherwise we open a new session; a case analysis shows the dominance relation is invariant under this transition).
- Transition: for each task `i` not in `mask`, if `tasks[i] ≤ remaining`, it goes into the current session `(s, r - tasks[i])`; otherwise a new session opens `(s + 1, sessionTime - tasks[i])`.
- Answer is the session count of the full mask.

Verification on examples:
- `[1,2,3], S=3` → 2 ✓ (e.g. order 1,2 | 3)
- `[3,1,3,1,1], S=8` → 2 ✓ (sum 9 > 8 so 1 impossible; 3,1,3,1 | 1 works)
- `[1,2,3,4,5], S=15` → 1 ✓ (sum = 15 fits exactly)

Complexity: `O(2^n · n)` ≈ 230K steps for n = 14 — very fast.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[] $tasks
     * @param Integer $sessionTime
     * @return Integer
     */
    function minSessions($tasks, $sessionTime) {
        $n = count($tasks);
        $size = 1 << $n;
        $full = $size - 1;
        $INF = PHP_INT_MAX;

        // dpS[mask] = min sessions used to finish tasks in mask
        // dpR[mask] = max remaining time in the current (last opened) session
        //             among all ways achieving dpS[mask]
        $dpS = array_fill(0, $size, $INF);
        $dpR = array_fill(0, $size, 0);
        $dpS[0] = 0;
        $dpR[0] = 0;

        for ($mask = 0; $mask < $size; $mask++) {
            $s = $dpS[$mask];
            if ($s === $INF) {
                continue;
            }
            $r = $dpR[$mask];
            for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
                $bit = 1 << $i;
                if (($mask & $bit) !== 0) {
                    continue;
                }
                $t = $tasks[$i];
                if ($t <= $r) {
                    $ns = $s;
                    $nr = $r - $t;
                } else {
                    $ns = $s + 1;
                    $nr = $sessionTime - $t;
                }
                $nm = $mask | $bit;
                if ($ns < $dpS[$nm] || ($ns === $dpS[$nm] && $nr > $dpR[$nm])) {
                    $dpS[$nm] = $ns;
                    $dpR[$nm] = $nr;
                }
            }
        }

        return $dpS[$full];
    }
}
```

