The problem is classic regular expression matching with '.' and '*'. Standard DP solution.

Let me write the DP:

dp[i][j] = whether s[0..i-1] matches p[0..j-1].

dp[0][0] = true.

dp[i][0] = false for i > 0.

dp[0][j]: if p[j-1] == '*', dp[0][j] = dp[0][j-2], else false.

Transition:
- if p[j-1] == '*' (and j >= 2): dp[i][j] = dp[i][j-2] OR (if match(s[i-1], p[j-2]) then dp[i-1][j]).
- else if match(s[i-1], p[j-1]) (p[j-1] == '.' or equal): dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1].
- else false.

match(a, b) = b == '.' || a == b.

Implement in PHP:

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String $s
     * @param String $p
     * @return Boolean
     */
    function isMatch($s, $p) {
        $m = strlen($s);
        $n = strlen($p);
        $dp = array_fill(0, $m + 1, array_fill(0, $n + 1, false));
        $dp[0][0] = true;
        for ($j = 1; $j <= $n; $j++) {
            if ($p[$j - 1] === '*') {
                $dp[0][$j] = $dp[0][$j - 2];
            }
        }
        for ($i = 1; $i <= $m; $i++) {
            for ($j = 1; $j <= $n; $j++) {
                if ($p[$j - 1] === '*') {
                    // zero occurrences
