- Target length ≤ 15, so I can represent progress as a bitmask of covered positions (2^15 states).
- **Key insight:** For any state, the *first uncovered* position must be covered by some sticker containing that letter — so I only branch on stickers containing that letter (avoids exploring permutations of the same multiset).
- Applying a sticker greedily to uncovered positions is safe because capped multiset subtraction is commutative — the resulting state depends only on the multiset of stickers used, not order.
- Optimizations: compress letters to distinct target letters, drop stickers that are componentwise dominated by another sticker (any use of a dominated sticker can be replaced), and memoize per mask.

